WEBVTT

00:07:28.527 --> 00:07:32.698
trying to rebuild and design
this new kind of queer-owned online space.

00:07:32.698 --> 00:07:34.575
And as we continue creating this space,

00:07:34.617 --> 00:07:37.786
we're standing on the shoulders
of all those who've come before us.

00:07:37.828 --> 00:07:39.830
And while I don't think safe online spaces

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.416
can solve all the problems
that queer communities face,

00:07:42.458 --> 00:07:45.169
I do think that being able
to gather safely in community,

00:07:45.169 --> 00:07:47.171
collect stories and share resources

00:07:47.171 --> 00:07:49.340
is leading to noteworthy changes.

00:07:49.381 --> 00:07:50.508
For example,

00:07:50.549 --> 00:07:53.886
most of the queer organizations
operating across the African continent,

00:07:53.928 --> 00:07:57.097
especially in contexts
where it’s illegal to be queer,

00:07:57.139 --> 00:07:59.975
use social media
to identify people in need,